# Project: Personal portfolio website (Chakri)

## Stack
- Next.js (App Router) with TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS for all styling (no CSS-in-JS, no component libraries unless I ask)
- Fonts via next/font (Inter or Geist, one family only)
- Deployed on Vercel

## Design rules (strict)
- Minimal and attractive. Dark theme only for now.
- Colors (define as CSS variables and Tailwind theme tokens, never hardcode hex in components):
  - background: #0A0A0A
  - foreground (main text): #F5F5F4
  - muted (secondary text): #A1A1AA
  - border: #27272A
  - accent (yellow): #FACC15
- Yellow is the ONLY accent color. Use it sparingly (links, hover states, buttons, one highlighted word in a headline). It should cover roughly 5% of any screen.
- Text on a yellow background must be near-black. Never use yellow text for long paragraphs.
- No gradients, no heavy shadows, no animated backgrounds, no skill-percentage bars.
- Use 1px borders (border color token) for separation.
- One centered content column, max width about 720px, generous whitespace and line spacing.
- Hierarchy through font size and weight, not extra colors.
- Hover effects: subtle only (underline, or fade to accent).
- Mobile first. Everything must look good at 375px wide.

## Code rules
- Use server components by default. Add "use client" only when state or browser APIs are needed.
- Keep components small and in /components. Pages go in /app.
- Keep project data in /data/projects.ts as a typed array for now.
- Use semantic HTML (header, nav, main, section, footer) and proper heading order.
- Add alt text for images and accessible labels for links and buttons.
- Prefer simple, readable code over clever code. Add short comments only where logic is not obvious.
- Do not install new dependencies without telling me why.

## Working style
- Make one change at a time. Do not rewrite unrelated files.
- Briefly explain what you changed and why, so I can learn from it.
